#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091898 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f5afc63-6988-5676-b170-5826e659a5fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-144" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y = 2x^3 - 2x$ at the point $(1,0)$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x) = 2x^3 - 2x\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative $f'(x)$ gives\n\n$$\nf'(x) = 6x^2-2\n$$\n\nWe then compute $f'(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\nf'(1) = 6(1)^2-2 = 4\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=4$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,0)$, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 0 &= 4(x - 1) \\\\\ny &= 4x - 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091899 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e248bb90-ba83-5e3f-938b-2c8be7d6eb7a" :question/math-academy-id "e-146" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt{x}+4x$ at the point $(1,8)$ intersects the $x$-axis." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)=4\\sqrt{x}+4x\n$$\n\nLet's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime }(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(4\\sqrt{x} + 4x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(4x^{1/2} + 4x) \\\\\n&= 2x^{-1/2} + 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1) = 2(1)^{-1/2}+4 = 6\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny - y_{1} &= m(x - x_{1}) \\\\\ny - 8 &= 6(x - 1) \\\\\ny &= 6x - 6 + 8 \\\\\ny &= 6x + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $x$-axis, we set $y=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0 &= 6x + 2 \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{1}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac 1 3, 0\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb2236bd-68b3-59f4-ad16-844d12efab36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089149} {:answer/id #uuid "ef3e4209-6488-5b46-a7db-bec5049b2485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089150} {:answer/id #uuid "53e45116-7b64-5dd3-af3b-2ab3dd83bb57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089151} {:answer/id #uuid "64b2dd3f-2d7d-5df3-a1fe-b10a02215842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089152} {:answer/id #uuid "78a5b430-34ca-52c7-8974-cdff5b8e2ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb2236bd-68b3-59f4-ad16-844d12efab36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089149} :answer-field/id #uuid "e491d2c8-ae2a-5467-ac5d-e8d2e6336eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b75358e5-0e2f-554f-8ca2-4e81d5f869f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-10831" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y = \\frac{5}{x} - 2x$ at the point $(1, 3)$ intersects the $y$-axis." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $5/x-2x$ is $-5/x^2-2$, giving slope $-7$ at $x=1$. The tangent is\n$$y-3=-7(x-1),\\qquad y=-7x+10.$$\nSetting $x=0$ gives the $y$-intercept $(0,10)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afabd727-147c-50f6-a917-420b7070f1fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=14x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243543} {:answer/id #uuid "e10f4f96-c77c-559b-9068-b0f0e4357599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=14x-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243544} {:answer/id #uuid "01892a33-5e8c-5801-8e91-88e95063021f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=7x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243545} {:answer/id #uuid "812432c7-aae7-5a83-9341-4409bef9ddf5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=7x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243546} {:answer/id #uuid "24bb9692-04b9-5402-9905-4aada8d316a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2x-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afabd727-147c-50f6-a917-420b7070f1fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=14x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243543} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b6e00d9-66a4-5a35-a450-c692d5cc0b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8eed30ff-0254-5346-9105-1abcf394d3fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-10837" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=5{x}^{2}+4x$ at the point $(1,9).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=5{x}^{2}+4x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2}+4x)=10x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=10(1)+4=14\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=14$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,9),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(9) & =14(x-1) \\\\ y & =14x-14+9 \\\\ y & =14x-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bdab51-0147-5c8b-b94e-2041f82148a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243550} {:answer/id #uuid "387fb26a-4e48-5d6b-9255-3ca5eccbb7e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-7x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243551} {:answer/id #uuid "5c16cc39-de34-5f61-a84a-61a9ef3004bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=6x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243552} {:answer/id #uuid "ca42379d-7f88-5ea1-911e-c18d0f47196e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243553} {:answer/id #uuid "bab51252-132e-534d-a533-853576db4230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-7x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bab51252-132e-534d-a533-853576db4230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-7x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243554} :answer-field/id #uuid "27deb4de-d4b9-5cff-b0ef-0adbaeb6e1dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "193a75aa-4f94-519d-96f9-e023967170ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-10839" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{2}-3x$ at the point $(-2,10).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}-3x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-3x)=2x-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(-2)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-2)=2(-2)-3=-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=-7$ and the coordinates of our point $(-2,10),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(10) & =-7(x-(-2)) \\\\ y-10 & =-7(x+2) \\\\ y & =-7x-14+10 \\\\ y & =-7x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84503a51-60f5-50ac-8980-6acef0742c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243557} {:answer/id #uuid "2297580a-178f-5cdc-85f6-f46595aee86a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243558} {:answer/id #uuid "a0443d82-56ed-539e-aa3d-a614d2638075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243559} {:answer/id #uuid "117ec70f-6564-5998-874b-5a35d8109afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243560} {:answer/id #uuid "002c1d3b-b850-5ea1-aec2-53feb52e2759" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84503a51-60f5-50ac-8980-6acef0742c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243557} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb4dc901-3ae4-5e02-9c7a-d48747e51481" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243556}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7368e613-bb1f-5cb2-ac24-2ec824bcacc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-10841" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{2}-6x$ at the point $(3,-9).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}-6x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-6x)=2x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(3)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3)=2(3)-6=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=0$ and the coordinates of our point $(3,-9),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-9) & =0(x-3) \\\\ y & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab980c55-c12d-5fb6-9789-b5fc7b6a54ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243564} {:answer/id #uuid "e79ee688-008e-5e02-b127-c180132956aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243565} {:answer/id #uuid "41e52791-4f04-5105-a6df-3d4cee449839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243566} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d29286-ff59-5770-8d25-9bc0988f9f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243567} {:answer/id #uuid "dc772fe7-1324-5027-bf0a-8d233e12c13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab980c55-c12d-5fb6-9789-b5fc7b6a54ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-3x+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243564} :answer-field/id #uuid "47482bac-a9de-5b00-af1f-2913ae2e4650" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243563}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88d07886-4d1e-5870-a644-8ea1806855a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-10845" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}+7x$ at the point $(1,9).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}+7x.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{5}}+7x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-5}+7x) \\\\  & =-10{x}^{-6}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(1)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1)=-10(1{)}^{-6}+7=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=-3$ and the coordinates of our point $(1,9),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(9) & =-3(x-1) \\\\ y & =-3x+3+9 \\\\ y & =-3x+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d507d0-340d-5078-bf7c-81166bcf902e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243571} {:answer/id #uuid "78cc7ee4-05a1-5daa-9eac-bce5ae3be9e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78cc7ee4-05a1-5daa-9eac-bce5ae3be9e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243572} :answer-field/id #uuid "a843db39-7c78-587a-8d82-b933b84b4cc4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243570} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1ba1433-4af8-59fd-9b6b-481a3eea28d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1ba1433-4af8-59fd-9b6b-481a3eea28d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243574} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ead8a6d-45aa-590a-9cd5-208f392b486c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "065e9604-fa49-5d1e-97d2-7ea5636842cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-304090" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=4x-{x}^{2}$ at the point  $(1,3)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $y$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=4x-{x}^{2}.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =4-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(1)=4-2(1)=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =2(x-1) \\\\ y & =2x-2+3 \\\\ y & =2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2(0)+1 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db808f48-6d0c-5b35-9342-b1817df65172" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Equation of a Tangent Line to a Curve at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e629624-0acf-5467-9cf2-d1187d2ce9f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e629624-0acf-5467-9cf2-d1187d2ce9f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243577} :answer-field/id #uuid "974c793b-3d07-5517-946e-8468b4b17481" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8675848b-359e-5358-9ed8-913d5be71171" :question/math-academy-id "q-342363" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt[3]{x}$ at the point $(8,8).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=4\\sqrt[3]{x}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt[3]{x}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt[3]{x}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-2/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(8)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(8) & =\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt[3]{{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt[3]{64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=\\frac{1}{3}$ and the coordinates of our point $(8,8),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-8 & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-8) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}x-\\frac{8}{3}+8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c64f9f04-ecfa-5cf3-8eda-0f68d9ad030b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c64f9f04-ecfa-5cf3-8eda-0f68d9ad030b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243580} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd45ea3b-1471-5dba-be81-73c443879475" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243579} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd1acad2-f0fe-525c-8652-e0b8f403f375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd1acad2-f0fe-525c-8652-e0b8f403f375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243582} :answer-field/id #uuid "b583525f-1e84-5cc9-a3cd-89e399a4235e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243581}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0da41f90-fa12-5c48-97e3-9f5af174c4d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-342377" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=\\frac{2}{x}+x$ at the point  $(2,3)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $y$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\frac{2}{x}+x.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{-1})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-2}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{2}^{2}}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{4}+1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-1+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}(0)+2 \\\\ y & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243583 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c545b39-b9ff-51ab-8caf-82da656c835a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243585} {:answer/id #uuid "bf40c181-630d-5501-b3d8-4eb636e69ca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c545b39-b9ff-51ab-8caf-82da656c835a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243585} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca77e8de-3c50-543a-8e83-140af27526e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb1dd618-c830-53be-8911-3190b6bdf9a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb1dd618-c830-53be-8911-3190b6bdf9a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243588} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a0ab9dd-4e4a-5811-8205-125ba522e619" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fbe0283f-22e7-53a8-b4f7-b07d4936416a" :question/math-academy-id "q-342379" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=-2\\sqrt{x}$ at the point  $(4,-4)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-2\\sqrt{x}.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-4) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-4) \\\\ y+4 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2-4 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $x$-axis, we set $y=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}x-2 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =-2 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(-4,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243589 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "84c8ba29-95c9-5494-be0b-9b67bee6e45c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining where a Tangent Line Intersects an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8d87bba-be48-528a-9962-6d47fab533ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8d87bba-be48-528a-9962-6d47fab533ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243591} :answer-field/id #uuid "d903a737-5156-5f34-aae6-45a8845d4d0e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243590} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3b196b9-e364-5805-b77c-b0f3b211a844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3b196b9-e364-5805-b77c-b0f3b211a844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243593} :answer-field/id #uuid "b89c3483-164c-5f89-b0ea-79f656408f92" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243592}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ab8d2aab-354f-5dc2-82dc-fb8380f780da" :question/math-academy-id "q-342381" :question/problem "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}$ at the point  $(4,5)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $y$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2})+6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}+6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{4}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-5 & =-\\frac{1}{8}(x-4) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{8}x+\\frac{1}{2}+5 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{8}x+\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{8}(0)+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,\\frac{11}{2}).$"}]}
